    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0675" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg601"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Tassara.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 8, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reply to your several recent
                    notes, relative to the case of the steamer Meteor and her detention at New York,
                    I have the honor to state that a report has been received by me from the United
                    States attorney in that city, from which it appears that all proper and
                    necessary steps have been taken by him to prevent any infraction of the
                    neutrality laws of the United States.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to offer to you renewed assurances of my highest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Don Gabriel Garcia y Tassara</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
